WEBVTT

00:03.420 --> 00:05.460
About a hundred years ago.

00:06.320 --> 00:10.420
This? Why this is
the story of a little girl,

00:10.480 --> 00:13.140
who travelled beyond the Door of Destiny.

00:16.640 --> 00:17.440
- NAAJA
- Nadja,

00:18.000 --> 00:19.270
With your eyes

00:19.271 --> 00:20.539
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:21.753 --> 00:22.880
What do you see?

00:22.881 --> 00:24.010
Nani ga mieru

00:24.210 --> 00:25.650
Shining in the far distance,

00:25.651 --> 00:27.090
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.220 --> 00:28.325
The door to the future,

00:28.326 --> 00:29.430
Mirai no tobira

00:30.320 --> 00:31.940
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.941 --> 00:33.560
Sagashite iru

00:33.820 --> 00:40.880
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:33.820 --> 00:40.880
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.660 --> 00:43.540
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:43.541 --> 00:45.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.920 --> 00:50.525
It could be so much more fun

00:50.526 --> 00:52.130
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.210 --> 00:53.920
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:53.921 --> 00:55.630
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.050 --> 00:57.700
I can't see the end of the journey

00:57.701 --> 00:59.350
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.443 --> 01:07.500
I will go waving

01:07.501 --> 01:08.560
Te wo furinagara

01:08.860 --> 01:12.175
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:12.176 --> 01:15.489
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.490 --> 01:16.845
But I won't look back

01:16.846 --> 01:18.200
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.450 --> 01:20.930
Until the day my dream comes true

01:20.931 --> 01:23.410
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.660 --> 01:25.370
Nadja, Your smile

01:25.371 --> 01:27.079
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.080 --> 01:28.750
Nadja, gives me courage

01:28.751 --> 01:30.420
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.630 --> 01:32.090
Under the blue sky,

01:32.091 --> 01:33.549
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.550 --> 01:34.965
I will find the place

01:34.966 --> 01:36.380
Ashita no yukue

01:36.970 --> 01:38.785
where my future lies

01:38.786 --> 01:40.600
Mitsukeru kara

01:48.040 --> 01:53.400
London

02:23.920 --> 02:25.700
I had a good night's sleep...

02:28.540 --> 02:29.540
Alright!

02:29.820 --> 02:30.820
Now then...

02:35.120 --> 02:36.120
"Mechanical"?

02:37.260 --> 02:40.620
The Dandelion Troupe, famous
for its mechanical automobile!

02:42.020 --> 02:44.200
Wow, mechanical, eh?

02:50.330 --> 02:54.180
Samurai Kennosuke's Wild Ride!!

02:54.240 --> 02:58.220
Vienna

02:59.700 --> 03:00.700
Come in.

03:02.020 --> 03:05.880
Master, we've received a telegram
from the detective in London.

03:06.240 --> 03:07.240
Read it.

03:07.360 --> 03:08.360
Yes, sir.

03:11.570 --> 03:15.350
"Discovered Lady Nadja at Applefield."

03:15.400 --> 03:18.460
"Whereabouts unknown,
due to a fire at an orphanage."

03:18.520 --> 03:20.320
"Currently conducting
further investigation."

03:28.540 --> 03:31.560
My deepest sympathies, Master.

03:33.240 --> 03:37.160
Please reply to the detectives, and tell
them to continue with their investigation.

03:37.220 --> 03:42.060
London

03:42.380 --> 03:43.640
Hey, Rosso.

03:43.960 --> 03:46.140
You reported to the Duke
what really happened.

03:46.280 --> 03:48.020
Won't Lord Herman be angry?

03:48.300 --> 03:49.860
He won't know.

03:50.140 --> 03:53.300
Besides, we get money
from the Duke's side too.

03:53.760 --> 03:56.200
Sometimes we have to give
proper reports too, you know...

03:56.760 --> 03:57.800
I guess so...

04:01.920 --> 04:02.920
Here you go!

04:10.340 --> 04:17.220
Hello, hello, how are
you, people of England?

04:17.360 --> 04:24.000
Bonjour, bonjour, how
are you, people of France?

04:24.280 --> 04:24.820
Please.

04:24.840 --> 04:29.859
Buenas tardes, how
are you, people of Spain?

04:29.860 --> 04:31.640
The Dandelion Troupe will be performing...

04:31.641 --> 04:38.060
Buon giorno, buon giorno,
how are you people of Italy?

04:31.680 --> 04:36.100
in front of the British
Museum starting tomorrow!

04:36.200 --> 04:38.279
Everyone, come one,
come all, and take a look!

04:38.280 --> 04:40.260
Lalala-lala, lalala-lala, la...

04:55.720 --> 04:57.200
Stephanie, where's Harvey?

04:59.740 --> 05:01.740
Sleeping off his hangover, again?

05:02.020 --> 05:03.780
That damn American!

05:08.080 --> 05:09.600
Harvey, wake up!

05:10.500 --> 05:14.340
Uh... Ten more minutes... no, just
let me sleep for another five minutes...

05:17.560 --> 05:19.840
Wake up! Harvey Livingston!!!

05:22.500 --> 05:24.180
Woah! Geez!

05:26.720 --> 05:29.840
That was mean, Chief Pratney.

05:30.220 --> 05:32.420
I'm chasing the Black Rose...

05:32.640 --> 05:35.800
going East and West, giving
up my sleep to gather material.

05:36.100 --> 05:36.800
Oh-ho?

05:37.060 --> 05:40.710
I didn't know you were
so dedicated to your job!

05:43.320 --> 05:46.280
Black Rose hasn't appeared at all lately.

05:47.000 --> 05:48.860
Maybe he moved his hideout...

05:49.300 --> 05:51.840
from London to Paris with
its exciting World's Fair?

05:52.200 --> 05:54.220
Will you cut it out with this nonsense!

05:54.360 --> 05:57.080
Can you please not talk so loud...?

05:57.200 --> 05:58.200
Look at this!

05:59.140 --> 06:03.020
Geez... That Black Rose struck again...

06:03.440 --> 06:05.140
The press all have extensive reports...

06:05.200 --> 06:08.040
on their front pages! All except for us!

06:08.480 --> 06:11.059
I understand! I'm off to the London police!

06:11.060 --> 06:12.220
You don't need to go.

06:13.540 --> 06:15.940
I'm taking you off the Black Rose case.

06:16.600 --> 06:17.660
Huh?

06:18.420 --> 06:19.980
Go get some material on this instead.

06:22.360 --> 06:24.740
The Dandelion Troupe?

06:38.440 --> 06:39.520
What's the matter?

06:44.720 --> 06:45.720
Eat?

06:45.860 --> 06:47.940
Oh, they're hungry!

06:54.680 --> 06:56.680
Rita, let's take a little break.

07:01.140 --> 07:02.140
Rita!

07:03.100 --> 07:04.660
I'll put your tea here.

07:19.420 --> 07:20.920
It's good...

07:23.900 --> 07:24.900
Eh?!

07:26.840 --> 07:28.420
What It's just tea...

07:29.080 --> 07:30.600
Ah! What the...!

07:30.820 --> 07:31.820
Say...

07:31.860 --> 07:33.900
Ew! He reeks of alcohol.

07:34.060 --> 07:37.480
Why do the English drink tea all the time?

07:37.880 --> 07:40.140
It should be coffee in
the morning, right? Coffee!

07:41.220 --> 07:44.160
You're such a rude fellow!
Just who the heck are you?

07:44.280 --> 07:48.060
Oh sorry, sorry. This is who I am.

07:48.440 --> 07:51.340
We will keep your coat for 10 shillings.

07:51.500 --> 07:53.280
Kensington Branch Shop.

07:53.440 --> 07:55.740
Aah! That's my pawn ticket!

07:56.120 --> 07:58.460
Let's see... Ah, here it is.

07:59.080 --> 08:02.140
Monmartre Journal, Harvey Livingston?

08:02.820 --> 08:04.640
You're a journalist for a French newspaper.

08:04.880 --> 08:07.640
Yeah, but I'm an American.

08:07.860 --> 08:08.860
Anyway...

08:11.160 --> 08:13.500
I wish to speak with the troupe master.

08:15.320 --> 08:16.320
Ah? Is that it?

08:18.280 --> 08:20.180
I see the mechanical automobile!

08:20.920 --> 08:22.640
Aren't there any adults around?

08:23.360 --> 08:24.600
Oh well.

08:25.380 --> 08:26.380
It can't be helped.

08:27.000 --> 08:28.240
You'll have to do, little lady.

08:28.360 --> 08:31.860
Can you tell me what motivated
you guys to perform in London?

08:32.160 --> 08:35.500
I... just joined the
troupe yesterday, so...

08:36.920 --> 08:37.920
Ah, I see.

08:38.900 --> 08:40.736
Well, that little lady
over there will be fine too.

08:40.760 --> 08:42.460
Rita is mute...!

08:42.740 --> 08:44.920
Ah...! I-I see...

08:45.820 --> 08:48.480
Damn it! That damned cheif...!

08:49.380 --> 08:53.500
I was taken off the Black Rose
case for something like this...!?

08:53.820 --> 08:55.460
What? Black Rose?

08:56.380 --> 08:59.880
Hmm? Ah, it's nothing. I'll come by again.

09:02.440 --> 09:05.320
Damn it, I wonder if
today is Friday the 13th.

09:06.220 --> 09:07.220
See ya!

09:07.940 --> 09:09.040
W-Wait a minute!

09:09.260 --> 09:11.000
Please don't just litter around carelessly!

09:11.360 --> 09:12.360
Geez...

09:12.860 --> 09:14.320
It's huge!!

09:14.980 --> 09:18.640
I've seen automibles in Paris, but this
is the first time I've seen one this huge.

09:33.760 --> 09:35.720
How do you make it into a stage?

09:48.300 --> 09:50.620
Why did it move all of a sudden?

09:50.800 --> 09:52.420
Eh...? A thief?

09:52.840 --> 09:54.560
W-What the?

09:54.600 --> 09:56.080
Stop!!!

10:18.720 --> 10:20.660
Rita! This is bad!

10:21.940 --> 10:23.720
What do I do to stop this?

10:23.980 --> 10:25.260
Out of the way, out of the way!!

10:25.400 --> 10:28.120
Watch out! Out of the waaaaay!

10:33.180 --> 10:34.360
Waaait!

10:37.440 --> 10:38.440
I'm sorry!

10:38.760 --> 10:39.980
Are you hurt?

10:40.520 --> 10:41.520
I'm all right.

10:46.500 --> 10:47.780
Madam, here.

10:48.200 --> 10:50.620
I'm in a hurry, so people excuse me.

10:54.440 --> 10:58.140
Lady Nadja should be about the
age of that yound lady, shouldn't she?

10:58.540 --> 10:59.840
Which reminds me...

11:00.020 --> 11:03.040
I wonder if that trunk
made it to the orphanage?

11:25.860 --> 11:27.080
What did you say?

11:27.580 --> 11:30.240
There was a fire at Applefield Orphanage?

11:30.800 --> 11:32.420
Then... what about Lady Nadja?

11:32.860 --> 11:34.260
C-Could it be...?

11:34.500 --> 11:37.740
Please do not worry, Miss Edna.

11:38.100 --> 11:40.180
Ah... she's all right then?

11:40.380 --> 11:42.820
Well, she's safe in a way...

11:44.740 --> 11:47.060
She left a letter with the principal...

11:47.280 --> 11:49.900
and disappeared without a trace.

11:50.360 --> 11:51.520
What did you say?

11:51.940 --> 11:56.130
That's why we thought you, the
nursemaid who gave her to the orphanage...

11:56.180 --> 11:59.180
might know where she was.

11:59.300 --> 12:00.400
I don't know.

12:01.200 --> 12:01.740
Really...

12:01.960 --> 12:05.400
I was planning to see Lady Nadja...

12:05.440 --> 12:07.580
on her coming thirteenth birthday, too.

12:08.080 --> 12:09.180
Is that so?

12:09.620 --> 12:11.620
Speaking of which, why is the Master...

12:11.700 --> 12:14.100
No, I mean, why is Duke Preminger...

12:14.380 --> 12:16.900
looking for Lady Nadja?

12:17.280 --> 12:21.860
I'm sure you know that his son,
Lord Herman, has many problems.

12:26.980 --> 12:28.160
I see.

12:32.680 --> 12:35.180
If you find out anything about Lady Nadja,

12:35.200 --> 12:37.700
will you please contact us here?

12:38.020 --> 12:39.320
Understood.

12:39.680 --> 12:41.620
That's it for now. Please excuse us.

12:45.480 --> 12:47.900
Ah, ah, aaah? Out of the way!

12:54.160 --> 12:55.300
You idiot!

12:57.120 --> 12:59.560
How the heck do I stop thiiiis?!

13:06.280 --> 13:07.520
It's not this. How about this?

13:15.100 --> 13:16.100
Well now.

13:16.140 --> 13:18.760
Now that we're done
drinking, let's get back to work.

13:18.980 --> 13:19.980
Okay. Yes.

13:23.180 --> 13:24.960
It's going! It's going!

13:25.340 --> 13:28.200
It looks more effective
than our efforts to advertise.

13:33.540 --> 13:35.560
By the way, who's driving it?

13:36.020 --> 13:39.420
W-We're all here, aren't we...

13:44.640 --> 13:46.940
What's up with this car?!

13:49.380 --> 13:51.920
Uh-oh... Someone's on board...

13:56.880 --> 13:58.520
What's up with these things?

13:58.540 --> 14:00.380
What did I do?

14:04.100 --> 14:07.900
Uh, I mean... it just started
to move when I touched it.

14:14.100 --> 14:16.900
Hey, how do you stop this?
Do you know how to stop it?

14:21.580 --> 14:23.080
W-what?

14:39.120 --> 14:40.120
Are you all right?

14:43.560 --> 14:44.560
I'm sorry.

14:44.760 --> 14:45.760
Umm...

14:46.400 --> 14:50.020
Err, I'm called Kennosuke. You?

14:55.080 --> 14:57.760
Eh? Ah... you can't speak...?

15:01.140 --> 15:03.380
I'm sorry. That was
an insensitive question.

15:16.780 --> 15:18.840
Whew! That was close!

15:26.140 --> 15:28.200
I was working hard on a stakeout.

15:28.880 --> 15:32.760
But, I got taken off the
Black Rose investigation.

15:33.880 --> 15:36.840
Hey, hey, I said that
we should leave early...

15:37.000 --> 15:39.180
But you were the one who
kept drinking until morning.

15:46.720 --> 15:48.400
Oh? Isn't that...

15:52.920 --> 15:54.960
What's that strange automobile?

15:55.220 --> 15:58.080
The Dandelion Troupe's
mechanical automobile...

15:58.660 --> 16:00.020
Someone!

16:01.040 --> 16:02.140
Stop that...

16:02.820 --> 16:03.820
car!

16:03.900 --> 16:05.440
Huh? Aren't you...

16:06.120 --> 16:09.820
Ah? It was an automobile
theif! Rita's still aboard!

16:10.200 --> 16:10.860
What?

16:11.000 --> 16:11.580
Harvey!

16:11.860 --> 16:12.860
Yeah.

16:13.480 --> 16:15.240
Hey! Stop, sto-

16:18.540 --> 16:19.740
That was dangerous!

16:19.860 --> 16:21.660
We're in a hurry, lend us your carriage!

16:21.820 --> 16:22.820
Get on!

16:23.320 --> 16:24.320
What the hell?

16:24.580 --> 16:25.840
I won't let you do this!

16:25.900 --> 16:27.300
It's a matter of human life!

16:27.540 --> 16:30.260
I'll return your carriage later at
the address on this calling card.

16:35.100 --> 16:38.360
We will keep your coat for 10 shillings.

16:38.900 --> 16:39.900
What the hell is this?

16:44.340 --> 16:47.060
Out of the way! Get out of the way, please!

16:49.260 --> 16:52.700
If this goes on, I might have no choice but
to keep driving until it runs out of fuel.

16:53.400 --> 16:56.600
Even so, this car is really fun.

16:57.160 --> 16:59.180
I wonder if it has any
other mechanical devices...

16:59.920 --> 17:01.080
What does this do?

17:08.340 --> 17:10.540
Way to go, you bastard thief!

17:11.040 --> 17:13.340
This will be a big scoop indeed!

17:14.580 --> 17:16.220
Looks like luck has finally come our way!

17:16.300 --> 17:17.300
That's mean!

17:18.060 --> 17:19.440
That's just mean!

17:20.260 --> 17:23.780
I'm sure Rita's scared... This
isn't the time to be laughing, is it?

17:26.660 --> 17:29.080
Please! Hurry up and save Rita!

17:32.200 --> 17:33.700
I'm sorry, little lady.

17:35.240 --> 17:37.640
I guarantee you... I'll stop that car!

17:48.980 --> 17:51.020
Goood! Just a little bit more!

17:53.420 --> 17:54.420
Rita!

17:55.060 --> 17:55.540
Eh?

17:55.620 --> 17:58.300
What the? The automobile thief is a kid?

17:58.720 --> 18:01.360
I had absolutely no intention of stealing!

18:01.920 --> 18:04.860
I just touched the car and
it started to move by itself!

18:05.200 --> 18:06.640
Rita, are you all right?

18:06.980 --> 18:07.980
Are you hurt anywhere?

18:09.580 --> 18:11.320
Hey, that's dangerous!

18:12.600 --> 18:14.840
It'll be bad if we don't stop it soon!

18:15.300 --> 18:16.680
Hey, stop that car!

18:16.980 --> 18:19.680
If I could I would have done it already!

18:20.180 --> 18:21.920
The brakes! Step on the brakes!

18:22.100 --> 18:24.300
Brakes? What... are those?

18:28.140 --> 18:29.360
So I just step on this?

18:33.600 --> 18:35.760
I-I'm stepping on it, but it's not moving!

18:36.880 --> 18:39.440
Mr. Reporter, please get closer to the car!

18:41.340 --> 18:42.500
You won't be able to do it!

18:42.560 --> 18:43.960
Just do it, quickly!

18:59.200 --> 19:00.560
Rita, don't move!

19:06.020 --> 19:07.660
Huey! Switch places with me!

19:18.260 --> 19:19.260
I can't...

19:26.680 --> 19:28.520
Waaah! It's the river!

19:28.640 --> 19:29.640
Out of the way!

19:36.820 --> 19:38.220
It's no use! We won't make it!

19:53.440 --> 19:54.460
We've stopped...

19:56.300 --> 19:59.360
Are you trying to drown my car?!

20:03.500 --> 20:04.540
Master!

20:14.580 --> 20:17.380
You really had no intention of stealing it?

20:18.160 --> 20:19.060
Of course!

20:19.100 --> 20:21.440
It's just that I love mechanics so much...

20:21.700 --> 20:25.360
It started moving when I
was examing how it worked...

20:27.020 --> 20:29.020
Boy, you like mechanics?

20:29.560 --> 20:32.740
Yes! I'm Kennosuke Tsurugi.

20:33.320 --> 20:34.600
Umm, Master, sir.

20:35.020 --> 20:37.540
Please let me join your troupe!

20:37.960 --> 20:41.260
Kennosuke? Hey! You're Japanese?

20:41.580 --> 20:42.160
Yes!

20:42.500 --> 20:45.780
I see! So you're from
the golden country, Japan!

20:46.260 --> 20:48.540
Kennosuke, do you have any special skills?

20:50.840 --> 20:52.620
- [iai-nuki, sword-art used for entertainment]
- I can do "iai-nuki."

20:53.000 --> 20:54.000
Iai-nuki?

20:54.420 --> 20:56.620
Oh? A samurai? That's interesting!

20:56.660 --> 20:58.120
Wait a minute, Master!

20:58.200 --> 20:59.640
Yeah, it's fine. Show us something.

21:21.240 --> 21:22.320
Mr Drunk Reporter.

21:22.720 --> 21:25.580
Hey. The pictures came
out so I came to show you.

21:26.460 --> 21:29.120
Oh? These are pretty good.

21:30.160 --> 21:32.296
It's going to be on the front
page of our newspaper tomorrow.

21:32.320 --> 21:34.800
So I'm sure everyone will
come to see your performance.

21:38.280 --> 21:39.760
And it's all thanks to Kennosuke!

21:40.320 --> 21:43.060
So it's decided, Kennosuke is in!

21:43.720 --> 21:45.040
Thanks very much!

21:48.120 --> 21:52.380
If even Rita likes him,
we can't say no, can we?

21:56.440 --> 21:57.980
I'll do my best!

22:01.140 --> 22:03.240
The Dandelion Troupe, huh?

22:14.490 --> 22:16.115
Paris is sunnier than London

22:16.116 --> 22:17.740
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.370 --> 22:24.455
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:24.456 --> 22:27.540
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.500 --> 22:37.065
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.066 --> 22:38.630
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.890 --> 22:41.245
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:41.246 --> 22:43.600
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:45.390 --> 22:47.895
The tree fog won

22:47.896 --> 22:50.400
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.860 --> 22:52.820
The world frog-jumping contest

22:52.821 --> 22:54.780
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.990 --> 23:01.075
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.076 --> 23:04.160
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.580 --> 23:07.665
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:07.666 --> 23:10.750
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.590 --> 23:15.255
Paris is sunnier than London

23:15.256 --> 23:16.920
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.510 --> 23:23.700
It's not the time to hang around

23:23.701 --> 23:26.890
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.770 --> 23:30.020
Indeed, indeed

23:30.021 --> 23:32.270
Kitto kitto

23:39.980 --> 23:41.960
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:43.380 --> 23:45.600
The long awaited first
performance in London.

23:46.420 --> 23:48.760
Ah! I'm so very excited.

23:49.720 --> 23:53.540
I met an interesting person
who said my dance was fantastic.

23:54.620 --> 23:56.900
Christian, who knows
everything about mummies.

23:57.700 --> 23:59.960
From the beginning of
our first conversation,

24:00.040 --> 24:01.740
it was all mummies, mummies, mummies!

24:02.620 --> 24:03.340
<i>Tomorrow's Nadja:</i>

24:03.360 --> 24:05.640
Dancing Princess Nadja
and The Mummy Professor.

24:06.671 --> 24:08.400
Now, the Door of Destiny opens.
